faqs:[
["Should I trust the body-fat percentage from my smart scale?","Use it cautiously as an estimate and prioritize consistent trends. It is not equivalent to a direct clinical or laboratory measurement."],
["What time should I use a smart scale?","Choose a time and routine you can repeat consistently; many people prefer similar morning conditions, but the key principle is standardization."],
["Why did my body-fat percentage rise overnight?","Changes in hydration and measurement conditions can move an impedance estimate without representing a comparable increase in body fat."],
["Should I ignore body weight and use body-fat percentage instead?","No. Body weight is directly measured by the scale and can be a useful trend metric; body-fat estimates add information but also add uncertainty."]
]
